## Typography Scale
```
Page title:       text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight
Section heading:  text-lg font-bold
Card title:       text-base font-semibold
Body text:        text-sm leading-relaxed
Meta/captions:    text-xs text-[var(--gn-text-muted)]
Section labels:   text-[0.6rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--gn-text-muted)]
Helper text:      text-[11px] text-[var(--gn-text-muted)] leading-relaxed
```

---

## Interaction Patterns

- Hover: `hover:bg-[var(--gn-surface-hover)]` — subtle green-tinted lift
- Focus: `ring-2 ring-[var(--gn-ring-focus)]` — green ring
- Active: `active:scale-[0.97]` — micro press
- Transitions: `transition-all duration-150` — snappy, not sluggish
- Empty states: friendly illustration-style with a plant emoji or leaf icon, never just "No items found"
- Loading: shimmer skeleton, never blank white
- Toasts: `sonner` — success=green, error=red, never orange

---

## What "sterile" means (what to avoid)

- ❌ `divide-y` list rows — use spaced cards with hover states
- ❌ Solid color backgrounds with no depth — use `surface-raised/elevated` layering
- ❌ Text-only pages with no visual anchors — add community icons, user avatars, plant photos
- ❌ Corporate gray palette — this is a GROW community, greens/ambers/natural tones
- ❌ Orange as primary brand color — it's a fast-food color, not a grow community
- ❌ Empty space with no CTAs or engagement prompts
- ❌ Plain letter avatars on gray circles — use the hash-based color palette
- ❌ Modals for everything — use inline actions where possible

---

## Admin Panel Rules

- Admin = Refine.dev + Ant Design, dark mode via ConfigProvider `colorPrimary: "#4ade80"` (dark) / `"#15803d"` (light)
- Dashboard must show live stat cards (open reports, communities, members) — never just redirect
- All list pages: visible search, icon preview, direct "View Public" links, status badges
- One-click moderation: approve/ban/pin/dismiss without drilling into sub-pages
- Admin sees everything; moderators see scoped moderation queue only

---

## Agent Checklist (before writing any frontend code)

1. Open the live site: `https://growersnotebook.com` — take a screenshot
2. Read the component file you're about to change
3. Ask: does this match the design system above?
4. Use ONLY CSS variables — zero hardcoded hex colors
5. Dark mode first — light mode must also work (use CSS vars)
6. No orange except fire/hot indicators
7. After changes: run `pnpm --filter @growers/web exec tsc --noEmit`
8. Fix all TypeScript errors before committing
9. Commit and push — changes that stay local are considered incomplete
